                        


Item #:  SCP-5279

Object Class:  Safe

Special Containment Procedures:  SCP-5279-1 is placed on a 4 meter high slab of concrete and kept there for 24 hours a day, 4 days a week with exceptions of testing from Level 2 and above research personnel whenever that might occur. It’s also noted that any persons that come into contact with SCP-5279-1 and SCP-5279-2 shouldn’t be wearing green, black, or anything shiny like a ring as wearing such could effect standard testing procedure.

Description:  SCP-5279-1 is a small seemingly indestructible cardboard box that houses SCP-5279-2, testing shows it’s resistant to fire, gunfire, blunt force, high caliber explosions, and even being doused in lava. Besides SCP-5279-1’s inability to be destroyed or even damaged, the box appears to have no other unusual effects and simply acts as a casing for SCP-5279-2.

SCP-5279-2 is a small black spherical rubber ball with the logo “Coca-Cola” branded on the front, upon research of the ball it was discovered that the company Coca-Cola had never actually made a rubber ball product before and that it was hand crafted.

SCP-5279-2 can be destroyed and damaged, however 24 hours after it’s originally damaged will seemingly regenerate in SCP-5279-1 even if totally obliterated.

While SCP-5279-2 is black in a dormant state, it will start flashing the colors of the rainbow once something black, green, or shiny enters 2 feet within the radius of SCP-5279-2 or SCP-5279-1, this will now be referenced as a “trigger event”.

Exactly 3 minutes and 47 seconds after a trigger event occurs 1-2 people within a mile radius of SCP-5279-2 will instantly die of either heart attack or extreme malnutrition, then SCP-5279-2 will revert back to a black color.

If there are no persons present after 3 minutes and 47 seconds into the trigger event, then SCP-5279-2 will go back to a dormant state and revert back to being black.

                    

                                    





            
    

                    



                    
                        
                            
